      r1_d: 'Whatever has been archived stays in the archive, even if it later disappears from the mailbox.',
      r1_t: 'Deleted by accident – on one device, and through syncing on all the others',
      why_col_answer: 'What MailArchy does about it',
      why_col_risk: 'What can happen',
      why_p2: 'Many people also don’t realise that their emails – especially when read on a phone – are stored only on the provider’s servers. Then there is no copy of their own anywhere.',
      why_p1: 'Email programs and mailboxes – Outlook, Thunderbird, Gmail or your provider’s webmail – are made for reading and writing, not for keeping emails for good. What gets deleted there is usually gone for good. And that happens more often through a slip of the hand than through a technical fault.',
      why_title: 'Why an archive? A mailbox is not a backup.',
