      shot_caption: 'Real interface, made-up demo data.',
      promises_title: 'Four principles that apply to every version',
      p1_t: 'Nothing is ever deleted from your mailbox',
      p1_d: 'MailArchy only reads. There is no function that deletes, moves or marks messages as read on the server – automated tests check this for every release.',
      p2_t: 'Your archive stays on your PC',
      p2_d: 'No cloud, no account, no telemetry. Nothing leaves your computer unless you explicitly want it to.',
      p3_t: 'Every email comes back byte for byte',
      p3_d: "Stored compressed, attachments kept only once – and still restorable exactly as it arrived. Export as EML, MBOX or PDF at any time.",
      p4_t: 'Updates never lose data',
      p4_d: 'New versions come signed from this site. Everything is backed up before a change; if something fails to start, MailArchy returns to the previous version on its own.',
      privacy_page: 'This website, too, sets no cookies, uses no tracking pixels and loads nothing from other servers.',
      features_title: 'Features at a glance',
      f1_t: 'All the usual sources', f1_d: "IMAP and POP3 (Gmail with Google sign-in, Yahoo, GMX, T-Online …) with automatic setup, Outlook files (.pst/.ost) even without Outlook installed, Thunderbird, EML and MBOX files.",
      f2_t: 'Archives on its own', f2_d: 'A schedule per mailbox, runs in the notification area, catches up on missed runs and emails you if something goes wrong.',
      f3_t: 'Encrypted if you like', f3_d: 'The whole archive protected with AES-256 – with your password, plus a recovery key for emergencies.',
      f4_t: 'Safe to view', f4_d: 'External images and tracking pixels stay blocked, scripts never run.',
      f5_t: 'On your phone at home', f5_d: 'Optional read-only web access for family members – everyone sees only the mailboxes you share.',
      f6_t: 'AI assistant, if you want', f6_d: 'Ask your archive in your own words (“Which contracts are still running?”) – with your own Claude key and sources for every statement. Without a key, everything stays local.',
      f7_t: 'Export any time', f7_d: "Single emails, folders or the whole archive as EML, MBOX or PDF – for printing, as proof or for another program.",
      f8_t: 'Light, dark, four languages', f8_d: 'Follows your Windows setting and contrast theme; English, German, French and Spanish.',
      open_title: 'Open source, developed with the help of AI',
      open_p1: 'MailArchy is “vibe-coded”: the program was developed in dialogue with an AI, Claude by Anthropic. A human decided what MailArchy should and should not do; the AI wrote a large part of the code.',
      open_p2: 'That is why the entire source code is public on GitHub. You can verify that MailArchy deletes nothing from your mailbox: anyone can read the tests that ensure exactly that, and run them.',
      open_repo: 'View the source on GitHub', open_board: 'Contributions on GitHub are welcome',
