      support_title: 'Support MailArchy',
      support_p1: 'MailArchy is free and will stay free. If you like, a contribution helps the developer pay for the server and further development.',
      support_p2: 'Contributing changes nothing: you get the same app as everyone else, no account, no unlocking, no ads. It is not a price for a service but a voluntary contribution.',
      support_btn: 'Support with PayPal',
      receipt_title: 'Need a confirmation?',
      receipt_p1: 'On request you get a payment confirmation with date, amount and the provider details from the legal notice. Just send the PayPal transaction number to <a href="mailto:mailarchy@zerze.de">mailarchy@zerze.de</a> after paying.',
      receipt_p2: 'No VAT shown: the contribution is voluntary and not linked to anything in return. MailArchy is not a charity, so a donation receipt is not possible.',
      faq_title: 'Frequently asked questions',
      q1: 'Does MailArchy need an internet connection?', a1: 'Only to fetch emails from mailboxes and to look for updates (can be turned off). Searching, reading and exporting work completely offline.',
      q2: 'Where is my data stored?', a2: 'In a folder of your choice on your PC – to back it up, simply copy the folder. Using the ZIP with a file portable.txt next to MailVault.exe keeps everything in the program folder, for example on a USB stick.',
      q7: 'Why does Windows warn me on first start?', a7: 'SmartScreen does not yet know programs without a purchased signing certificate, so it warns. You can read what is in the setup in the open source code on GitHub. After that, MailArchy verifies updates itself using a signature.',
      q3: 'Does Gmail work with two-step verification?', a3: "Yes. The easiest way is to sign in to MailArchy with your Google account – then no password is needed in MailArchy. Alternatively, use an app password from your Google account. Both are explained in the guides above.",
      q4: 'Is there MailArchy for Mac or Linux?', a4: 'No, MailArchy runs on Windows 10 and 11. The web access on your home network works with any browser though, including Mac, iPhone and Android.',
      q5: 'What happens to my emails with the AI assistant?', a5: 'Nothing, as long as you do not switch it on. With your own Claude key, only the excerpts needed to answer your question are sent to Anthropic – you see every source.',
      q6: 'How do I remove MailArchy?', a6: 'Quit MailArchy, then delete the folder %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\MailVault and the Start menu shortcut – done, no admin rights needed. Your archive is stored separately and stays until you delete it yourself.',
      q9: "Was MailArchy previously called MailVault?", a9: "Yes. Up to version 0.7 the program was called MailVault. It is the same program with the same archive: existing installations get the new name automatically with the next update, and your emails and settings stay where they are.",
